√śas (śásati; śaśā́sa; śasiṣyáti; śastá;
-śásya). cut to pieces; slaughter. [see
śastra.]

śāstrá, n.
 —1. instruction;
 —2. rule;
theory; compendium (of an art or
science); a scientific or canonical work;
science, 17^13. [√śās.]

śā́sana, n.
 —1. government, way of ruling;
 —2. command. [√śās.]
